WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.840
Write h as the sum of h
sub j times X to the j.

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:07.880
Its star is the sum of h sub
k times X to the negative k.

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:13.160
Multiply these sums: each pair
contributes h sub j times h sub k,

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:17.560
at exponent j minus k.
Exponents are read modulo n.

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:23.280
In a four-position illustration, arrange
the sixteen pairwise products in a grid.

00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:28.450
Each entry belongs to the coefficient
indexed by j minus k modulo four.

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:30.460
To collect a single coefficient,

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:34.200
select exactly those cells
with the same exponent.

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:36.880
Fix an exponent a.

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:42.840
A term contributes to X to the a precisely
when j minus k is congruent to a modulo n.

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:47.080
Equivalently, k is j minus a modulo n.

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:52.440
Thus the coefficient of X to the a
in h times h star is the sum, over j,

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:56.880
of h sub j times h sub j minus a.

00:00:57.740 --> 00:01:04.060
But h sub j minus a is the jth entry
of the row shifted a places right.

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:07.940
Our coefficient is therefore the
dot product of the original row with

00:01:07.940 --> 00:01:11.960
that shifted row. The coefficient
notation always refers to the

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:14.720
unique representative
of degree less than n.

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:19.080
Check the original row,
negative one, one, one, one.

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:24.940
Shift zero gives dot product four. Shifts
one, two, and three each give zero:

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:28.600
two negative contributions cancel
two positive contributions.

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:32.240
So the product has
coefficients four, zero,

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:36.740
zero, zero, and equals the
constant polynomial four.

00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:41.720
For general n, collect every
exponent in the same way.

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:47.820
The product h times h star is the sum over
a of the cyclic correlation at shift a,

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:53.280
times X to the a. This identity works
for arbitrary integer coefficients.

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:57.620
For sign coefficients, the
constant correlation is n.

00:01:58.460 --> 00:02:01.340
That extra hypothesis enters
in the Hadamard dictionary.
